; 7 - Numbers, '#', FCB lists, FCS, RMB
; Numbers: $1F hex, %0101 binary, 42 decimal, 'A' character.
; A number runs to the end of the word; every digit must fit the base.
;
; Try it:
;   - Hover over the errors: the message often suggests the correction.
;   - Line 22: "FCB 1,2 3,4" - the blank ends the operand, "3,4"
;     silently becomes a comment. Remove the blank.

            ORG     $20
            FCB     $1F,%0101,42,'A' ; OK
            FCB     0a              ; ERROR: decimal with a letter - suggests $0A
            FCB     0x1F            ; ERROR: C notation - suggests $1F
            FCB     %000200100      ; ERROR: 2 is not a binary digit
            FCB     $FG             ; ERROR: G is not a hex digit
            FCB     $               ; ERROR: $ without digits
            FCB     255,-256        ; OK: limits of a byte
            FCB     256             ; ERROR: too big
            FCB     -257            ; ERROR: too small
            FCB     -129            ; OK: qaflisp silently takes $7F
            FCB     200+100         ; ERROR: the result 300 is too big
            FCB     1,2 3,4         ; WARNING: blank inside the list
            FCB     1,2, 3,4        ; ERROR: the list ends with a comma
            FCB     1,,2            ; ERROR: value missing between the commas
K           EQU     #5              ; ERROR: directives take no #
            ORG     #$40            ; ERROR: directives take no #
            LDA     2+#1            ; ERROR: # only at the start
            FCS     "OK"            ; OK
            FCS     ""              ; ERROR: empty string
            RMB     0               ; ERROR: RMB needs at least 1
            RMB     -1              ; ERROR: negative
A$b         NOP                     ; OK: qaflisp allows $ and . in a label
NOP                                 ; WARNING: missing indent - only a label, no code
            ORG     $100            ; WARNING: outside the memory
